# Per-device isolation.
#
# A device's MQTT username is set to its topic serial (the <serial> in
# Enertek/<serial>/...). This one pattern rule therefore confines EVERY device
# to its own serial's topics — no device can read or write another's. This is
# the fix for the cross-tenant exposure in Enertek's broker.
pattern readwrite Enertek/%u/#

# A monitoring/control client (Home Assistant, the app) on a SINGLE-user
# self-hosted broker can simply authenticate as the device's serial — it then
# shares the same (own-device-only) scope.
#
# For a MULTI-tenant / hosted broker, give operator or per-user accounts their
# own explicit rules instead of reusing a device serial, e.g.:
#   user my-dashboard
#   topic read Enertek/1234567890/#
